    {
      "text": "Lord spake unto Moses … as a man speaketh unto his friend, Ex. 33:11. thou hast spoken friendly unto thine handmaid, Ruth 2:13. the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, 1 Sam. 18:1. when Job’s three friends heard of all this evil, Job 2:11. have pity upon me, O ye my friends, Job 19:21. when he prayed for his friends, Job 42:10. mine own familiar friend … lifted up his heel, Ps. 41:9. rich hath many friends, Prov. 14:20. A friend loveth at all times, Prov. 17:17. a friend that sticketh closer than a brother, Prov. 18:24. Wealth maketh many friends, Prov. 19:4. Make no friendship with an angry man, Prov. 22:24. Faithful are the wounds of a friend, Prov. 27:6. a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend, Prov. 27:17. I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend, Isa. 41:8.",
