      "text": "a friend of publicans and sinners, Matt. 11:19 (Luke 7:34). he answered … Friend, I do thee no wrong, Matt. 20:13. Jesus said … Friend, wherefore art thou come, Matt. 26:50. Jesus … saith unto him, Go home to thy friends, Mark 5:19. because he is his friend, Luke 11:8. When thou makest a dinner … call not thy friends, Luke 14:12. Make to yourselves friends of the mammon of unrighteousness, Luke 16:9. betrayed both by parents … and friends, Luke 21:16. the same day Pilate and Herod were made friends, Luke 23:12. friend of the bridegroom … rejoiceth, John 3:29. Our friend Lazarus sleepeth, John 11:11. that a man lay down his life for his friends, John 15:13. If thou let this man go, thou art not Cæsar’s friend, John 19:12. gave him liberty to go unto his friends, Acts 27:3. Abraham … was called the Friend of God, James 2:23. friend of the world is the enemy of God, James 4:4.",
